#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This chapter describes how you can control the behavior of &quantaplus;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The configuration dialogs are accessible from the <guilabel>Settings</"
"guilabel> menu. Here we will discuss only few of them, the rest are not "
"&quantaplus; specific and a short description can be found at <xref linkend="
"\"settings-menu-3-2\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: config-quanta.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring Quanta"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The configuration dialog can be invoked by using "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenu>Configure Quanta...</"
"guimenu></menuchoice>. The dialog has several pages, we will discuss them "
"one by one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: config-quanta.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tag Style"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can change the behavior of &quantaplus; related to tags, including "
"autocompletion. The entries are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Tag case:</guilabel> the case of the automatically inserted tags. "
"<guilabel>Default Case</guilabel> means the tags will be inserted as they "
"are described in the <link linkend=\"tagxml-3-2\">tagXML</link> files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Attribute case:</guilabel> the case of the automatically inserted "
"attributes. <guilabel>Default Case</guilabel> means the attributes will be "
"inserted as they are described in the <link linkend=\"tagxml-3-2\">tagXML</"
"link> files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Attribute quotation:</guilabel> how to quote attributes inserted "
"by &quantaplus;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Auto-close optional tags:</guilabel> if checked, tags for which "
"closing tag is option will be automatically closed once the tag closing &gt; "
"is entered."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Auto-close non-single and non-optional tags:</guilabel> same as "
"before for the rest of tags, exception being the single tags."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Use auto-completion:</guilabel> turn on/off the autocompletion of "
"tags, attributes, functions, etc."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Update opening/closing tag automatically:</guilabel> if enabled, "
"whenever you change the opening tag, the corresponding closing tag will be "
"changed as well and vice-versa."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Automatic replacement of the accented characters:</guilabel> if "
"enabled the accented characters will be replaced with their codes as you "
"type."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: config-quanta.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid "Environment"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid "A page to control the environment and some default settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Mimetypes:</guilabel> mimetypes used to recognize different kind "
"of files. Use the <guilabel>Reset to Default</guilabel> button to fill in "
"the entries with the default settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Default character encoding:</guilabel> the encoding of the newly "
"created files, or files loaded in other way than <menuchoice><guimenu>File</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Open</guimenuitem></menuchoice> (where you can override "
"the encoding). This setting is overridden by the same setting in the "
"<guilabel>Project Properties</guilabel> if a project is loaded."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Default DTD:</guilabel> the DTD used for newly created files, or "
"files whose DTD was not recognized. This setting is overridden by the same "
"setting in the <guilabel>Project Properties</guilabel> if a project is "
"loaded."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Create backups:</guilabel> &quantaplus; will create backup files "
"periodically, so in case of power failure or crash, on the next startup the "
"document can be restored from this backup. This is not the same as the "
"backup created on file save. Even for not-yet saved documents there is a "
"backup created."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Startup Options:</guilabel> self explanatory setting which control "
"what will happen on startup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: config-quanta.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid "User Interface"
msgstr "Interfaç utilizaire"

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here you can control the look and feel of &quantaplus;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The preview and the documentation can appear in the editor area or in a "
"separate toolview, in which case it's possible to look at the documentation/"
"preview and the source as well."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It's also possible to configure the look of the toolview and document tabs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Reset window layout to the default on the next startup</guilabel> "
"is useful when you have messed up the user interface by changing the MDI "
"modes and docking/undocking the toolviews. It is the same as the <command>--"
"resetlayout</command> command line switch."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is the place also to control the behavior of the file trees."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Warning Messages</guilabel> section is useful to enable or "
"disable the warning messages that can be dismissed by checking the "
"<guilabel>Do not show again</guilabel> box in them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: config-quanta.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid "VPL View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The place to change the &VPL; behavior. You can enable the showing of an "
"icon in place of scripts as well as configure the synchronization of the VPL "
"and source view when the splitted mode is activated. See <xref linkend="
"\"view-menu-3-2\"/> to learn how to activate the different modes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: config-quanta.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "Parser"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can fine-tune the parser and the structure tree, which is the "
"visual representation of the parser nodes in the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Clicks on Structure Tree Items</guilabel> it is possible to "
"change the actions assigned to mouse buttons when you click on the structure "
"tree."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Structure Tree Look &amp; Feel</guilabel> it is possible to "
"configure what kind of nodes are visible in the tree, how often is the tree "
"updated while editing and on an update how deeply should be the structure "
"tree automatically opened. Empty nodes are the white-space text nodes, while "
"empty groups are groups for whom there was no element found in the current "
"document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: config-quanta.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid "Abbreviations"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The place to define abbreviations (some kind of templates), that can be "
"expanded to bigger text while editing. Abbreviations are organized in "
"groups, each group can be valid for more than one &DTEP;. This means you can "
"have a group valid for PHP where the \"ifclause\" abbreviation template "
"means something else than in a group valid for JavaScript."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: config-quanta.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring Actions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"User defineable action creation and editing is described in <xref linkend="
"\"user-actions\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: config-quanta.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring Plugins"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can manage your plugins. Plugins are KPart applications written by "
"third parties that can be reused in any KPart aware application, the most "
"known being &konqueror;. When creating a plugin you must specify the:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Name:</guilabel> the user visible name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Output window:</guilabel> plugins can appear in a tab of the "
"editor area or in a separate toolview at the bottom"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Location:</guilabel> the path to the plugin, if it is not located "
"in the standard locations, like <filename class=\"directory\">"
"$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/lib</filename> ."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>File name:</guilabel> the relative path and the filename to the "
"plugin's libtool file, like <filename class=\"libraryfile\">kde3/"
"libcervisiapart.la</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Input:</guilabel> the plugin will get this information on startup, "
"so it can open the <guilabel>Current File</guilabel>, the folder of the "
"current file (<guilabel>Current File Path</guilabel>) or the "
"<guilabel>Project Folder</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Read only part:</guilabel> check if the plugin refuses to load. "
"Read-only KParts usually refuse to load without this option checked."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Validate plugin:</guilabel> if checked, &quantaplus; will test if "
"the entered information is correct or not. Uncheck if the plugin is not yet "
"available, but you will install later, so you can close the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: config-quanta.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"See <xref linkend=\"plugins-menu-3-2\"/> and <xref linkend=\"kparts-3-2\"/> "
"for information about using the plugins."
msgstr ""
